^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-02-20 01:54] observe — The codebase often relies on DOM `data-` attributes for styling hooks and state transport between different components or CSS selectors.
 >>[2026-02-20 01:54] decide — This audit will locate all ad-hoc `setAttribute('data-...')` calls, formalize them into reactive properties if they belong to custom elements, or define a standard update utility if they are imperative global states.
 >>[2026-02-20 05:30] revise — Expanded plan to 26 commits to emphasize taste development through state machine refactoring and ARIA semantic synchronization.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:15] observe — plan-ecology sweep: every predicted path targets src/ui/elements/, which no longer exists in this repo. src/ now holds only runtime, seed, and testing shims. This plan is stranded on a deleted layout, not in progress — disposition (relocate to a site repo, re-scope against packages/, or archive as superseded) is a user call.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:31] observe — re-ground: the live data-* surface is the installable-book init preset in the CLI templates. enhancements.js writes body dataset js and online and reads data-include, data-install-app, data-refresh-site, data-dismiss-notice; the CSS reads only data-spw-region and data-spw-affect, and a grep of the preset finds no reader of data-js or data-online.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:31] revise — commits trimmed from the copied 26 to ~[1], ~[3], ~[26]; ~[2] and ~[4]..~[25] target src/ui/elements, src/platform, and src/app/dom-sync, none of which exist, and are marked DROPPED. Disposition stays a human call, tracked in hygiene-index-consolidation ?[stranded_fate].
 >>[2026-10-12 14:57] decide — User decided on 2026-10-12 to rescope this plan rather than archive it
 >>[2026-10-12 14:57] observe — Correction to the 14:31 note: the CSS also reads data-spw-container, and the nav value of data-spw-region has no rule. data-edit-surface appears 17 times in the HTML and nothing in the repo reads it. showUpdateNotice builds a notice with no role or aria-live. html.js-enhanced .js-only sets display initial, which may override the hidden attribute on the install button; the wonder carries the probe and I did not run it.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:57] revise — Rescoped to planning on the installable-book hooks: goal is a checked data-* contract plus an announced update notice. Commits are now 1 to 5 starting with a contract test. The old dependency on refactor-import-sprawl is dropped. Old 1 2 3 4 to 26 moved to done as dropped. Two questions open.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:36] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 0 landed, 5 planned, 4 dropped.
}

^["open"]{
 # Unresolved questions. When resolved: log in stream, then move to ^["done"] as ~#resolved(label).
 ?[edit_surface_owner]: "Is data-edit-surface (17 occurrences in the preset HTML, read by nothing in the repo) a contract with an outside editor or consumer site, or leftover scaffolding? Unblocks ~[resolve_edit_surface]: document it as inert, or strip it."
 ?[online_marker]: "Should body data-online drive a visible offline marker in style.css, or should the dataset writes in enhancements.js go? Unblocks ~[resolve_online_marker]."
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[hook_contract_test]: "![cli] — add installable-book-hooks.test.ts: every data-* name under public/ is read by enhancements.js or the CSS, or listed in an explicit inert set; every name enhancements.js queries appears in some page"
 ~[announce_update_notice]: "&[cli] — mark the update notice built in showUpdateNotice with role=status so assistive tech announces it"
 ~[resolve_online_marker]: "&[cli] — resolve data-js and data-online per ?[online_marker]: add the CSS reader or delete the two dataset writes, and update the inert set"
 ~[resolve_edit_surface]: "&[cli] — resolve data-edit-surface per ?[edit_surface_owner]: keep it in the declared inert set with a one-line owner note, or strip it from the nine HTML pages"
 ~[hide_install_button]: "&[cli] — keep the install button hidden until beforeinstallprompt, only if the install-button wonder confirms html.js-enhanced .js-only overrides [hidden]"
}

