 ~#resolved(css_readers): "Which data-* names does the CSS read? — the 14:31 stream note was incomplete: data-spw-region (hero, main, footer rules in style.css; the nav value, written 9 times, has no rule), data-spw-affect (five rules in substrate.css), and data-spw-container (four rules in substrate.css); evidence: grep of [data- in the preset CSS, 2026-10-12"
 ~#resolved(hook_catalog): "What data-* names does the preset write, and who reads them? — in the public/ HTML pages: data-spw-region 26 (footer 9, nav 9, main 7, hero 1), data-spw-container 14, data-spw-affect 8, data-edit-surface 17 (9 distinct values, no reader), data-include 16 (read by hydrateFragments), data-install-app 1 (read by enhancements.js); data-refresh-site and data-dismiss-notice are created by showUpdateNotice and read by its own listeners; evidence: grep -o over public/*.html, 2026-10-12"
}

#>wonder_audit_data_attributes_install_button
?["Does the Install app button show on a page load where beforeinstallprompt never fires?"]{
  #:depth #!computational // lens: reflection contract
  ~#hypothesis: "yes: index.html marks it hidden, but html.js-enhanced .js-only sets display: initial with higher specificity than the user-agent [hidden] rule, so the button is visible as soon as enhancements.js runs"
  !probe{ "serve packages/spw-cli/templates/init/presets/installable-book/public with any static server, load / in a browser that has not met install criteria, and read getComputedStyle(document.querySelector('[data-install-app]')).display; 'none' falsifies the hypothesis" }
  $%[plan.commit_count, plan.phase_progress]
}
